    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d399">

                <pb facs="0492" n="1326" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1326"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 659.119/243</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Denmark</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Grant-Smith</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Copenhagen</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-03-22T12:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 22, 1918, noon.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 9.06 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2073. Referring to the Legation’s No. 2072, 22d. Our British and French
                    colleagues concur in the opinion that the importation into Denmark of the
                    commodities designed to relieve Danish unemployment before the conclusion of the
                    negotiations now in progress would sensibly weaken our position and consequently
                    jeopardize their consummation.</p>
                <closer>[<signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Grant-Smith</hi>
                    </signed>]</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
